{%- comment -%}
  Cards-only view of a collection, used by the product page to pull "more parts
  that fit this vehicle" from a tag-filtered URL:

      /collections/all/chrysler-300?view=cards

  Shopify's Section Rendering API returns 404 on this store, so this is how the
  product page gets real, vehicle-matched cards without duplicating card markup
  in JavaScript. `layout none` keeps the response to just the cards.

  The current_tags guard matters: Shopify silently IGNORES a tag it does not
  recognise and serves the whole collection instead of 404ing. 180 parts carry a
  malformed vehicle tag from the yard system ("Dodge Dodge 1500"), and without
  this they would pull the head of the catalogue under a "fits your vehicle"
  heading — the exact bug this replaced. current_tags is empty in precisely that
  case, so render nothing and let the caller keep its own fallback.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- layout none -%}
{%- if current_tags.size > 0 -%}
  {%- for product in collection.products limit: 8 -%}
    {% render 'card-product', card_product: product %}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
